{
  "method": "POST",
  "path": "/api/v1/infection/waste/handover",
  "summary": "Hand collected waste over to the contractor",
  "tags": [
    "Infection prevention and control"
  ],
  "permissions": [
    "infection.waste.record"
  ],
  "permissions_mode": "all",
  "idempotency_key": true,
  "description": "The contractor's consignment note for waste weighed and recorded before it (MSDS IPC 88; backend issue #53): list\nwhat awaits it (`GET /infection/waste?awaiting_handover=true`), choose the collections the note covers and send them\nonce, with the contractor (`GET /finance/vendors?vendor_type=Contractor`), the note's number and the disposal. Each\ncollection is handed over whole and its weight is never entered again; the totals' `handed_over_kg` follow. Send an\nIdempotency-Key: a retry after a lost answer gets the same answer, while the same collections sent again without it\nare refused.\n\n`WASTE_HANDED_OVER`: a collection already carries a consignment note (`details.waste_id`, `manifest_number`,\n`handed_over_on`), which is final. `REFERENCE_NOT_FOUND` (details.field): an unknown collection (`waste_ids`) or\ncontractor. `VALIDATION_ERROR`: a handover in the future, or before a collection's day.\n\n**Required permission:** `infection.waste.record`\n\n**Required permission:** `infection.waste.record`",
  "roles_allowed": [
    "ipc_nurse",
    "ops_admin"
  ],
  "parameters": [
    {
      "name": "Idempotency-Key",
      "in": "header",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Unique per logical action; retries return the first result",
      "schema": {
        "anyOf": [
          {
            "type": "string"
          },
          {
            "type": "null"
          }
        ],
        "description": "Unique per logical action; retries return the first result",
        "title": "Idempotency-Key"
      }
    }
  ],
